#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Manual installation notes for people who prefer the Arch way.
less -R <<'EOF'
Velocity Linux: manual install notes
====================================

Velocity is Arch Linux underneath. The Arch wiki installation guide applies
verbatim (https://wiki.archlinux.org/title/Installation_guide). Differences:

1. Bootstrap with the Velocity base set instead of plain `base`:
     pacstrap -K /mnt base linux linux-firmware velocity-tools

   `velocity-tools` provides the `velocity` customizer, the branding hook,
   and the preset library. Everything else is optional.

2. Inside the chroot, brand the system and pick a desktop:
     velocity brand apply
     velocity desktop set plasma      # or hyprland, gnome, xfce, core
     velocity theme set night         # or day

3. Bootloader: `velocity install-bootloader` wraps grub-install +
   grub-mkconfig with the Velocity theme.

Run `velocity-install` for the guided path that does all of this for you.
EOF
